---
name: sdlc-release
description: Finalize a target release, verify item statuses, and promote items to released status
globs: "docs/**/*"
---

# Command: /sdlc-release <version>

## Instructions
1. Locate `docs/releases/<version>.md` (e.g., `docs/releases/v1.0.0.md`).
2. Read all specs listed in the release table (features, bugs, experiments).
3. Verify that all listed specs have status `ready-for-release`. If any spec is not ready, warn the user.
4. For every listed spec:
   - Update Frontmatter status to `released`.
   - Update the status column in `docs/releases/<version>.md` to `released`.
5. Update release file Frontmatter:
   - Set `status: released`.
   - Set `released_at: <current-date>`.
6. Log official release publication in `docs/history.md`:
   `| <Timestamp> | Release | <version> Published | Released | docs/releases/<version>.md |`
7. Provide a concise, user-friendly summary of the published release.